WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.246
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:03.296 --> 00:00:06.069
Robotics 101, video 6.

3
00:00:06.119 --> 00:00:09.150
Building the robot body.

4
00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:11.307
Time to build.

5
00:00:11.357 --> 00:00:15.895
Clear your table, keep the screws in a small bowl, and ask

6
00:00:15.945 --> 00:00:18.900
an adult to help with the screwdriver.

7
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.782
Here is the plan from above.

8
00:00:22.832 --> 00:00:25.549
The two motors go at the back.

9
00:00:25.599 --> 00:00:28.223
The castor goes at the front.

10
00:00:28.273 --> 00:00:32.650
The sensors sit at the very front, looking down.

11
00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:37.329
First fix both motors with their brackets.

12
00:00:37.379 --> 00:00:39.941
Push the wheels onto the shafts.

13
00:00:39.991 --> 00:00:42.635
Screw the castor under the front.

14
00:00:42.685 --> 00:00:47.451
Mount the Arduino and the motor driver on top, then fix the

15
00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:49.900
battery holder and the switch.

16
00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:55.881
Mount the two sensors at the front, facing down, about five to

17
00:00:55.931 --> 00:00:58.297
ten millimetres above the floor.

18
00:00:58.347 --> 00:01:02.751
Space them a little wider than your black line, so the line

19
00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:04.110
fits between them.

20
00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:10.736
If the sensors are too close together, both see the line at once.

21
00:01:10.786 --> 00:01:16.483
If they are too far apart, the robot wobbles before it notices a turn.

22
00:01:16.533 --> 00:01:20.260
A gap a little wider than the line works well.

23
00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:30.622
Before you wire anything, check that the wheels spin freely, the robot

24
00:01:30.672 --> 00:01:34.670
sits level, nothing is loose, and the battery switch is off.

25
00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.514
Let us recap.

26
00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:41.712
Motors at the back, castor at the front.

27
00:01:41.762 --> 00:01:47.169
Sensors at the front, about 5–10 mm above the floor.

28
00:01:47.219 --> 00:01:51.052
Keep wires tidy and away from wheels.

29
00:01:51.102 --> 00:01:54.830
Next: Wiring the electronics safely.
